# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# aeon-music-video — environment variables
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pure-CPU tool. No ComfyUI, no GPU, no large models. Just ffmpeg + librosa.
# This file is mostly optional — defaults work fine for most users.
#
#   cp .env.example .env && $EDITOR .env && ./setup.sh
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. ffmpeg / ffprobe binary paths  (OPTIONAL — uses PATH lookup)
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This tool depends ENTIRELY on ffmpeg with the `sendcmd`, `eq`, `hue`,
# `rgbashift`, `gblur`, `showcqt`, `avectorscope`, `loudnorm`, and
# `acrossfade` filters — all standard in any modern build.
#
# Default behavior: rely on PATH. Override only if your binaries are at
# non-standard locations.
#
# Linux/macOS (probably already on PATH):
# FFMPEG=/usr/bin/ffmpeg
# FFPROBE=/usr/bin/ffprobe
#
# Windows (only if you installed ffmpeg to a custom path):
# FFMPEG=C:/ffmpeg/bin/ffmpeg.exe
# FFPROBE=C:/ffmpeg/bin/ffprobe.exe
#
# To install ffmpeg if you don't have it:
#   macOS:    brew install ffmpeg
#   Debian:   sudo apt install ffmpeg
#   Windows:  https://www.ffmpeg.org/download.html (use a static build)


# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. Default render parameters  (OPTIONAL)
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Override CLI defaults. Per-call --fps / --width / --height / --lufs flags
# always win over these.
#
# DEFAULT_FPS=24
# DEFAULT_WIDTH=832          # smooth compositor (reactive_compositor.py)
# DEFAULT_HEIGHT=480
# DMT_WIDTH=720              # vertical short-form (dmt_flash_editor.py)
# DMT_HEIGHT=1280
# DEFAULT_LUFS=-12.0         # loudness target for embedded audio


# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Note: this repo has NO ComfyUI dependency.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unlike aeon-music-maker, aeon-radio-drama, and aeon-movie-maker, this
# tool runs 100% on the local machine using ffmpeg + librosa for audio
# analysis. No GPU required, no models to download, no API calls.
#
# Input requirements:
#   - An audio file (any format ffmpeg reads): the song the video reacts to
#   - One or more video clips (any format ffmpeg reads): the source footage
#
# Output:
#   - An MP4 video where the visuals pulse, cut, and color-shift in time
#     with the audio
